  "recovery_latency_s": 184.49074792861938,
  "client_view_text": " A message that changes everything.\nThe lighthouse stood tall and proud on the rocky coast, its beam slicing through the darkness like a shining sword. Keeper James had lived in the tower for nigh on 20 years, watching the sea and the world go by from his solitary perch. He knew every wave, every tide, every storm that came and went. He knew the sea like the back of his hand.\nBut on this particular evening, as the sun dipped below the horizon, James noticed something peculiar. A bottle, half-buried in the sand, caught his eye. He picked it up, blowing off the grains of sand A message that changes his life forever.\nThe lighthouse keeper, Jack, had been stationed on the rocky coast for five years. He had grown accustomed to the solitude, the rhythmic sound of the waves, and the occasional visit from a passing ship. But on this particular day, something caught his eye. A bottle, half-buried in the sand, caught the morning sun and glinted like a tiny jewel. Jack walked over to investigate, his boots sinking into the damp sand.\n\nAs he picked up the bottle, he noticed it was old, the glass worn and weathered. He carefully removed the cork and peered inside. A piece of paper, yellowed with age, was tied to a small rock. Jack untied the paper and smoothed it out, revealing a message scrawled in hasty handwriting:\n\n\"Dear whoever finds this,\n\nMy name is Emily. I was on a ship that sank in a storm off this coast. I was the only survivor. I've been living on this island for months, but I'm running out of food and hope. If you find this, please know that I'm still alive. I'm hiding in a cave on the north side of the island. Please come for me.\n\nYours,\nEmily\"\n\n"
}